{"title":"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A piece of paper containing six joined squares labeled as shown in the diagram is folded along the edges of the squares to form a cube.  The label of the face opposite the face labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab8416f1514dce5c2c075749bfab240c1e34b68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,1)--(2,1)--(2,2)--(3,2)--(3,0)--(2,0)--(2,-2)--(1,-2)--(1,0)--cycle); draw((1,0)--(1,1)); draw((2,0)--(2,1)); draw((1,0)--(2,0)); draw((1,-1)--(2,-1)); draw((2,1)--(3,1)); label(&quot;U&quot;,(.5,.3),N); label(&quot;V&quot;,(1.5,.3),N); label(&quot;W&quot;,(2.5,.3),N); label(&quot;X&quot;,(1.5,-.7),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(2.5,1.3),N); label(&quot;Z&quot;,(1.5,-1.7),N); [/asy]\" width=\"188\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef7d5791b9b381003b76845250df97bb82dfca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{Z} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{U} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{V} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\ \\text{W} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"355\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that two faces of a cube are opposite each other if and only if they share no vertices.  The diagram shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> shares at least one vertex with each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e40e9753162902272463ac3891bf02979fdcdc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{U}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84747d5c85012db9b725a8e5b1d56d661160f16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{V}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f72bafb29c6f143901be25459b3984ed3fb2671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{W}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1007df3907ac8012f2fda920cd57d95b80bb2fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, so by process of elimination <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> must be opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe6997aadfa432bfa5640791496cae70ebbb24d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\  \\text{Y}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the face opposite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, we can find the faces sharing an edge with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, so the only face remaining will be the opposite face.\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84747d5c85012db9b725a8e5b1d56d661160f16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{V}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1007df3907ac8012f2fda920cd57d95b80bb2fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> share an edge with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.  Also, the faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84747d5c85012db9b725a8e5b1d56d661160f16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{V}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f72bafb29c6f143901be25459b3984ed3fb2671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{W}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> share a common vertex, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> shares an edge with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f72bafb29c6f143901be25459b3984ed3fb2671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{W}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.  Similarly, the faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e40e9753162902272463ac3891bf02979fdcdc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{U}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84747d5c85012db9b725a8e5b1d56d661160f16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{V}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> share a common vertex, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> shares an edge with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e40e9753162902272463ac3891bf02979fdcdc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{U}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.  \n</p><p>The only face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> doesn't share an edge with is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcfb65d98e3e4d7d8592056f225e7e1bddebf4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, which is choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d1302e73ece29d10218238af739577904f6f00a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YE9u_O5d-Eg\">https://youtu.be/YE9u_O5d-Eg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME\" title=\"1985 AJHSME\">1985 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"